<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="007" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-06: Enforce external grant expiry on every grant read path</title>
    <phase>0 Enforcement Remediation</phase>
    <gate>after-001</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs on an authorization path (grant read filter) — FULL per root CLAUDE.md §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Add an expiry predicate to enumerated read paths; the minimum fix is explicitly specified by the spec and D-1.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalParticipationService.cs — known contended path (Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/**; task 015 modifies AccessibleRecordSetService.cs in the same directory and both feed the same read pipeline).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, dataverse</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Close finding A-5 (spec FR-06, High): external grant expiry must be enforced. sprk_expiresdate is written at grant time but never read — it appears in no $filter and no $select on any read path, and there is no sweep job. A grant with an expiry date in the past currently confers full access forever, while the UI presents expiry as a working control (a promise-shaped no-op).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Dataverse Web API OData filtering and the external-access read pipeline (ExternalParticipationService / AccessibleRecordSetService). Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Every read path that materializes external grants excludes rows whose sprk_expiresdate is in the past. A grant with past expiry confers no access anywhere: participation queries, accessible-set composition, and effective-access views all treat it as inactive.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Finding A-5 (design-register §A.1): "sprk_expiresdate written, never read — absent from $filter and $select" — evidence ExternalParticipationService.cs:405-407 (the grant query filters `_sprk_contact_value eq {contactId}` + statecode only); only write-side refs exist repo-wide; no sweep job. Spec FR-06 acceptance: a grant with sprk_expiresdate in the past confers no access; if deferred, the expiry input must be removed from the UI — this task takes the ENFORCE branch (register D-1: "small — add to the read filter"). Enumerate ALL grant read paths: ExternalParticipationService.QueryGrantSetAsync and every sibling query in that service that materializes sprk_externalrecordaccess rows (grep for the entity set name across src/server). Evaluate expiry against UTC now, server-side in the OData $filter (expiresdate null OR &gt; utcNow), not client-side after materialization.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalParticipationService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/GrantLifecycleCharacterizationTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Characterization test pinning expired-grant-still-active behavior, flipped here.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed: a grant row whose expiry cannot be evaluated (query error) is NOT granted; malformed expiry data excludes the row. Scope: the expiry predicate added by this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The expiry predicate must be applied in the Dataverse $filter on EVERY read path that materializes grants — a single missed path silently re-opens the finding. The task is complete only when a grep for the sprk_externalrecordaccess entity set shows every read query carries the predicate (or is documented as non-access-conferring). Scope: all of src/server.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No sweep/deactivation job in this task — expiry is read-side enforcement only (register D-1 minimum; row cleanup is out of Phase 0 scope). Scope: this task adds no background work.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF-touching task (CLAUDE.md §10): report publish size vs ~44.96 MB baseline in PR; ceiling 60 MB (NFR-06). Scope: this task's PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>external grant read pipeline</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-003-authorization-seams.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/investigation/10-finding-confirmations.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/design-register.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="endpoint-definition" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md">OData query conventions in BFF services</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load knowledge files; declare FULL rigor.</step>
    <step order="1">Grep src/server for every read query against the sprk_externalrecordaccess entity set; produce the closed list of read paths (expect: ExternalParticipationService grant-set + participation queries; note ProjectClosureEndpoint reads are a revocation sweep, not access-conferring — leave to task 016).</step>
    <step order="2">Add `sprk_expiresdate` to $select and the predicate `(sprk_expiresdate eq null or sprk_expiresdate gt {utcNow})` to $filter on each access-conferring read path.</step>
    <step order="3">Verify the field's logical name against live Dataverse metadata before trusting docs (schema docs in this area are stale per design-register §G).</step>
    <step order="4">Flip the task-001 characterization test: expired grant now confers no access; add boundary tests (expiry exactly now / null expiry / future expiry).</step>
    <step order="5">Run full test suite; build green.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Record the closed read-path list + predicate placement in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the live logical name of the expiry field differs from sprk_expiresdate, STOP, verify against dev Dataverse metadata, and record the discrepancy — do not guess a column name into a security filter.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any read path cannot take a server-side predicate (e.g. FetchXML composed elsewhere), STOP and escalate the design rather than filtering client-side silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools><tool name="dotnet">Build + test</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalParticipationService.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/GrantLifecycleCharacterizationTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A grant with sprk_expiresdate in the past confers no access: the record is absent from the caller's participation/grant set (FR-06 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A grant with null expiry or future expiry confers access unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a contact whose ONLY grant on a record is expired is denied on that record (accessible-set + IsRecordAccessible seam).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The predicate is server-side ($filter), verified by inspecting the built query in tests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Closed list of sprk_externalrecordaccess read paths documented; each carries the predicate or a written non-access-conferring rationale.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit tests pass; build green; publish size reported in PR and ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-06; finding A-5; register D-1 (enforce branch chosen — UI input stays because it now works). No sweep job: expired rows remain in the table as inactive-by-read; Phase 5 attestation will see them.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
